00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.020
Sorry this video took so long -- I had never actually seen the Child's Play movies before,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.160
so I went ahead and binged them so that I
could properly analyse the trailer for you,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.570
and I'm now kind of realizing I probably didn't
have to, but I did notice some interesting

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.400
stuff in the trailer and the website setup
for the fictional company within the movie,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.420
so stick around to the end of this video if
you want to hear about it.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.260
The beginning of the  Child's Play trailer plays as a commercial
for this company Kaslan, a tech company that

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.779
makes coffee machines, robotic vacuum cleaners,
tablets, VR games, robots, and toys.

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:35.370
If it's been a while since you watched the
original series, the company behind that was

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.410
called Play Pals Toys, so this is not the same
company.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.040
All signs point to this being a re-imagining
of the original, so if the original had taken

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.060
place in the 10s or whatever the **** this
 decade is called, it this is how it

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.200
might have gone down.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.340
So the Good Guy dolls from the 1980s film
are now called Buddi, because for some reason

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:55.399
lower case 'i's are really popular this millenium,
I should probably just change my channel name

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:57.079
to be spelled like this.

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:00.879
Here's our new Andy Barclay, and in background
there's a photo of him and his father.

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:04.650
In the original Child's Play Andy does have
a deceased father, but we never really know

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.650
anything about him.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.390
When we first see Andy it appears that he's
rocking some wireless headphones, however,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.620
there's another shot later in the trailer
where it's evident that it's just his left

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.590
ear, and every time we see the left ear, it
has this device, which has to be his hearing

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.440
aid, because those are popular in horror movies now?

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.600
But in this movie, the hearing aid could be
subject to wireless interference from Chucky,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.930
as a new 21st century way for Chucky to attack
Andy.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.900
In fact, you can actually go to the website
on the side of the box, bestbuddi.com, where

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.190
there are more clues about Chucky's capabilities.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:43.760
It's emphasized in the logo, which contains
the wifi symbol, telling us that internet

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.390
connectivity play a big part in this new doll,
and it will connect with tablets, computers

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.840
and cell phones.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.460
Chucky is going to be connected to this Kaslan
ecosystem of smart devices, and I think the

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.350
horror in this movie is going to be a commentary
about how smart home devices are becoming

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.420
something we trust and rely on too much.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:04.460
Look at this text: Your new best friend connects
to and controls all your Kaslan products and

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.950
smart home devices.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.980
Not "you control your doll and your devices."

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.170
The doll is the one controlling the devices.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.170
This company is in control of your home and
your life.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.599
Look at this picture.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:18.770
Chucky has control over your computer, your
fans, and your sound system, which I'm sure

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.310
ties right back into the fact that Andy has
a hearing aid.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.379
He's also seen manipulating a smart TV, and
a drone, which brings to mind the scene from

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:30.680
Child's Play 3, where the CEO is attacked
by all the toys in his home, including an

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.810
RC helicopter.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.160
This website also suggests that Buddi uses
AI to interpret human behaviour, which makes

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.450
me think that instead of the Chucky doll being
possessed by voodoo, like it is in the original,

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.120
the doll will be "possessed" by hackers, who
load a malicious code into the Buddi doll.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.442
Maybe Charles Lee Ray is actually a cyber-criminal
in this movie.

00:02:47.442 --> 00:02:51.430
The last item of note on this website is the
fact that Buddi comes loaded with the ability

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.719
to communicate in English and Spanish.

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:57.370
Andy's mother is played by actress Aubrey
Plaza in this movie, who has a Puerto Rican

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:00.880
background, so her and her son aren't going
to be safe from eavesdropping by Chucky no

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.790
matter which language they are speaking.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.609
Let's talk about possible Easter Eggs.

00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:08.829
The warehouse of Buddi dolls bears great resemblance
to the Good Guy doll storage in the factory

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:10.510
at the end of Child's Play 2.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.680
The crime scene shows a covered body surrounded
by broken glass as if someone had fallen from

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.859
a window, which calls back to the original
Child's Play where Aunt Maggie becomes the

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.100
first victim of Chucky, at least in his doll
form.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.020
This might be the fall actually happening,
and you may notice the Kaslan logo on the

00:03:35.029 --> 00:03:39.440
truck in the background, meaning this accident
could have taken place at the factory or a

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.440
distributor.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.400
Whatever is going on here bring reminders
of Andy and Kyle in the factory scene from

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.629
Child's Play 2, and when Chucky initially
grabs the clothes, I noticed a drill on the

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:49.880
table, which is one of the weapons used in
Cult of Chucky.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.739
The movie will take place in the winter around
Christmas time like the original, although

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:57.080
it does not seem like they stuck with Chicago
for the setting unfortunately.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.629
I don't recognize this license plate, but
it's most similar to Idaho or a South Dakota

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:02.629
alternate.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:06.349
One thing I personally found interesting was the fact
that when Andy first unwraps the doll, we're

00:04:06.349 --> 00:04:10.510
seeing from Chucky's point of view, as if
he's already on and gathering information

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.209
before they even open the box.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:15.900
Now you may remember in the first movie, Chucky
had to go back to find Andy Barclay and take

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.220
over his body because he was the first one
Chucky revealed himself to.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.460
"You have to transfer your soul out of the
doll, into that of the first human being you

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.080
revealed your true self to."

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.050
So maybe in the new movie Chucky is programmed
to go after the owner of the doll, and the

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.080
facial recognition determines who that actually
is.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.800
Chucky is shown to be wielding his classic
knife in this movie...

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.520
"A true classic never goes out of style."

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.280
But there are some new modern weapons showcased
in this trailer, like the ability to turn

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.840
off the lights and give a new meaning to 'Black
Friday Shopping', and maybe even taking control

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.350
of a self driving car developed by Kaslan.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.490
At the end of the trailer, you're prompted
to click on this next video, which is a special

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:01.090
announcement video from the Kaslan Corporation,
which you may or may not have already noticed

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.090
that the logo contains a blue eye, just like
that of Chucky.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.830
The announcement features Henry Kaslan, the
founder of the Kaslan Corporation, and he

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.690
gives an introduction to the Buddi doll, saying
that every child deserves a companion.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.290
The video description confirms that Buddi
will use artificial intelligence and encourages

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.480
viewers to visit KaslanCorp.com . Visiting
the site reveals more information about the

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:23.700
company and their technology, like the use
of HD cameras, and a paragraph about other

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.700
sensors.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.420
It says, "Kaslan HUB and VR products come
equipped with state of the art haptic and

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:32.440
accelerator technology, to help you thrive
in the real world while also immersing you

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.520
in the in the imagination of the vast and
ever-evolving virtual reality landscape."

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.760
This means that Chucky's ability to hunt down
Andy has received a major upgrade, he'll have

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.780
the ability to learn the tendencies of Andy's
body movement to help him predict what his

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.640
